# Veridian — Build Spec

> **Veridian** is a meditative, infinite fidget. A 10-point star whose concentric rings respond to your touch like ripples — push, twist, pinch, breathe. Pocket calm.

The name comes from *viridian* (the deep blue-green of the metallic finish on the original physical toy that inspired this app) crossed with *meridian* (a center line, an axis, a moment of equilibrium). It's pronounceable, available, and trademarkable in the App Store / Play Store namespace at the time of this writing — you'll want to verify before submitting.

---

## 0. What this document is

A handoff spec to take the working HTML prototype (`star-fidget.html`) and turn it into a production-ready Expo app shippable to the iOS App Store, Google Play Store, and the web. It's written to be executable by Claude Code: each phase has explicit deliverables, acceptance criteria, and the exact CLI commands to run.

The prototype is the **source of truth for behavior**. The spec defines the **architecture** to support that behavior across three platforms.

---

## 1. Scope

### v1.0 ships with
- Single-screen fidget experience, fullscreen
- Single-touch joystick (lateral push + pull-up to extend)
- Two-finger twist + pinch (gesture composition)
- Spring-back physics with configurable params
- Floating, draggable Tuner panel (Photoshop-style)
- 4 named presets
- Settings persist locally between sessions
- iOS, Android, Web from one codebase

### v1.0 explicitly does NOT include
- Multi-handle / multi-puppet input *(deferred to v1.1 — own design pass)*
- Cloud sync of settings *(maybe v1.2)*
- Sound or audio reactivity
- Sharing screenshots/videos
- Onboarding tour beyond a single first-launch hint
- Accounts or auth of any kind

### Hard non-goals
- No analytics that aren't strictly anonymous (this is a meditative app; we should not be watching people)
- No ads, ever
- No notifications

