## 2. Tech stack — locked-in versions

Based on what's current as of May 2026:

| Layer | Choice | Version | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| Framework | Expo SDK | **55.x** | Latest stable (released Feb 25, 2026). Includes RN 0.83, New Architecture by default, Hermes. |
| Language | TypeScript | strict mode | Catches whole classes of bugs at compile time. |
| Routing | Expo Router | v6 (bundled w/ SDK 55) | One screen for now, but sets us up for settings page / about page without thinking. |
| Rendering | `@shopify/react-native-skia` | latest compatible | GPU-accelerated 2D drawing. Same fillPath + stroke approach as our HTML canvas, but native. Web build via CanvasKit. |
| Animation | `react-native-reanimated` v3 | bundled by Skia | Animation runs on UI thread via worklets — no JS bridge cost during gestures. Required by Skia. |
| Gestures | `react-native-gesture-handler` v2 | latest | Composable gesture system. Multi-touch for our twist/pinch. |
| State | `zustand` | latest | Tiny, no boilerplate. The slider params are global enough to justify a store. |
| Persistence | `expo-secure-store` for any future user data; `@react-native-async-storage/async-storage` for tuner params | latest | Async-storage is fine for non-sensitive settings; secure-store for future. |
| Haptics | `expo-haptics` | bundled | Subtle ticks on extension thresholds, gesture lock-in. |
| Build/submit | EAS Build + EAS Submit | current | Native builds in the cloud, submit to both stores from one command. |
| Web hosting | EAS Hosting (or Cloudflare Pages) | — | TBD; EAS Hosting is integrated but Cloudflare Pages is free and great. Decide at launch. |

### Project starter
```bash
npx create-expo-app@latest veridian --template with-skia
```
The `with-skia` template includes Reanimated, Gesture Handler, and Skia preconfigured for both native and web.

