## 5. Custom URL scheme — `veridian://`

Since v1 has no inbound deep links to handle, the scheme is mostly for future-proofing — sharing presets, opening from a system action, etc. Register it now so we don't have to deal with a re-review later.

In `app.json`:
```json
{
  "expo": {
    "scheme": "veridian"
  }
}
```

This makes `veridian://` openable on iOS and Android. For web, we'll use a regular URL (e.g. `veridian.app/preset/floaty`) once we own the domain.

**v1 routes claimed (even if not implemented yet):**
- `veridian://` — opens the app to the fidget
- `veridian://preset/<name>` — opens with a named preset loaded
- `veridian://share/<encoded-params>` — opens with a custom param set (basis of "share my fidget" feature in v1.1)

Document these in the README so we don't accidentally repurpose them.

